  "candidates": ["Z73.3", "F41.1", "F31.9"],
  "reason": "The patient describes a chronic, mild increase in restlessness and drive to stay busy that began in temporal association with an identifiable psychosocial stressor (financial and home-repair burdens) roughly 1.5 years ago. Systematic screening ruled out manic/hypomanic episode (no elevated mood, no decreased need for sleep, no grandiosity), generalized anxiety disorder (no excessive worry, no muscle tension, no autonomic symptoms), akathisia/restless legs syndrome (no new antipsychotic/antiemetic use, no dysesthesia in legs, no evening-predominant urge to move), and hyperthyroidism (no weight loss, tachycardia, tremor, heat intolerance). The restlessness is goal-directed (volunteering, tidying, being 'helpful') rather than distressing, and the patient explicitly denies irritability, anxiety, or significant functional impairment—she frames it as a personality trait exacerbated by stress rather than a discrete psychiatric syndrome. Although the original stressors have resolved, the behavior pattern persists as an ingrained coping habit, consistent with a residual stress-related adjustment pattern rather than a distinct anxiety, mood, or movement disorder. This clinical picture best fits Z73.3 (stress, not otherwise classified), representing a subclinical stress-response pattern rather than a diagnosable mental disorder.",
  "diagnostic_checklist": {
    "symptom_groups": [
      {
        "group": "restlessness/hyperactivity",
        "confirmed_symptoms": [
          "chronic feeling of needing to stay busy and move rather than sit still",
          "urge to get up and do something during quiet/sedentary periods (e.g., meetings, church)",
          "engagement in excessive volunteering and household tasks to stay occupied",
          "mild interpersonal friction due to over-involvement (asked to step back from a committee role)"
        ],
        "count": 4
      },
      {
        "group": "ruled_out_manic_symptoms",
        "confirmed_symptoms": [
          "denies elevated, euphoric, or abnormal mood",
          "denies decreased need for sleep",
          "denies grandiosity or irritability"
        ],
        "count": 0
      },
      {
        "group": "ruled_out_anxiety_symptoms",
        "confirmed_symptoms": [
          "denies excessive worry about health, family, or daily matters",
          "denies feeling keyed up, tense, or unable to relax",
          "denies autonomic symptoms (sweating, racing heart, tremor)"
        ],
        "count": 0
      },
      {
        "group": "ruled_out_medical/medication causes",
        "confirmed_symptoms": [
          "no new antipsychotic or antiemetic medication use",
          "no leg dysesthesia or evening-predominant urge to move legs (RLS negative)",
          "no weight loss, heat intolerance, or tachycardia (thyroid causes negative)"
        ],
        "count": 0
      }
    ],
    "duration_verified": "Restlessness/busyness pattern reported as noticeably present for approximately 1 year 5 months, initially associated with a psychosocial stressor (financial and home repair issues) and persisting after stressor resolution.",
